			"notes": "## SkyBlock Companion Beta 0.2\n### New Features\n+ Added places to the Item List: NPCs, bosses, mobs, places and warps, in a new World tab and in the search of All.\n   + Each one opens its own page, like an item: where it is and how far, the wiki's first lines about it, Navigate, its warp and the wiki.\n   + Right-click in the list guides you straight there with the path line.\n+ Added every Hunting shard to the Item List, with prices, search and their own item page.\n+ Added what an item really sold for to item tooltips: the median price of the last 3 days and how many sell a day, under the lowest BIN.\n   + Items with fewer than 3 sales show nothing, and the lines wait until there is a full day of sales.\n+ Added Analyzed mutations: a greenhouse mutation's tooltip says whether you have analyzed it.\n+ Added the Sack Helper beside the Sack of Sacks.\n   + Every kind of sack is one family of sizes.\n   + Missing lists what is left, cheapest first. Owned shows what you have and what it costs to finish.\n   + Your sacks come from your profile and from every sack you open in the menu.\n+ Added a What's new page after an update: everything since the version you played before, newest first.\n   + It shows the whole changelog of every version you skipped.\n   + New helpers stay off until you switch them on there. Nothing is turned on for you.\n   + `/sbc whatsnew` opens it again.\n+ Added a fast and a detailed setup. The fast one asks a few questions; the detailed one then shows every helper of what you play.\n   + Nothing is answered for you: every question starts open.\n   + Each helper's options and an example of its card are on the detailed pages.\n+ Added support for Minecraft 26.3.\n+ Added CurseForge to the update screen and Mod Menu, next to Modrinth and GitHub.\n### Improvements\n+ The dungeon map is now Hypixel's own map from your last hotbar slot, pixel for pixel, in the card's frame. Your teammates show as Hypixel draws them.\n   + You are an arrow at where you really stand, turning with your view, so it moves smoothly instead of waiting for the next map update.\n   + Every player Hypixel draws on the map shows on the card.\n+ The pet card follows summons, Autopet and despawns from chat, so it also knows your pet in dungeons, where the tab list has none.\n+ The Three Weirdos solver finds the right chest by the speaker's name, without waiting for the room to be matched.\n+ Secret routes say what to do at each spot: Pull lever, Mine (Dungeon Breaker), Superboom, Etherwarp or Pearl.\n   + A lever comes before its locked chest, an etherwarp is drawn as a jump, and a step moves on only when its secret is taken.\n   + A chest that opens with a lever: the route goes to that lever first, from the room's data, and a locked chest keeps the step until it is pulled.\n   + The normal route is the default.\n+ The player card takes your SkyBlock level from the tab list first, so a level up shows right away.\n+ The player card keeps the top left corner at its own size. The other cards fit around it instead of moving it.\n+ Networth keeps up on the player card and the profile page: your profile loads again every 5 minutes, and the card uses your purse and bank as they are now.\n+ Your profile page shows each skill as the game shows it when Hypixel's API is still behind.\n+ A maxed skill gets a gold card on the profile page. Levels past the cap are off unless you switch them on.\n+ A maxed skill is gold in Your Skills too.\n+ The vanilla XP bar and your level stay on screen. Hiding them is an option of the skill card.\n+ The Buy Helper starts folded, like the Item List, and opens by itself when its list gets something to buy.\n+ Party Finder, the pets screen and the browser open at the K menu's size instead of covering the whole screen.\n+ Switching loadout shows its equipment in the inventory at once.\n+ Protected items move freely in your own inventory and storage again: shift-click and number keys work.\n\n..."
		},
